          "why-0"
        ],
        "search_text": "When a critical power generation equipment failure triggered an equipment failure, the grid management authority faced a massive power deficit to overcome. The decisive crisis managers stepped in, ordering an emergency load shedding to keep a critical transmission line from overloading, a courageous decision to prevent total collapse. This action addressed the significant loss of generation capacity, leaving more than 950 megawatts unavailable as a high-level warning was issued across the frontline of the power crisis.",
